      "title": "Troubleshooting Bulk Import Stalls and Duplicate Accounts in Mobile App Provisioning",
      "content_summary": "Addresses scenarios where bulk user imports fail to complete or generate duplicate records, typically caused by schema mismatches during migration or invalid customer configuration.",
      "content_body": "1. Check the import logs for 'schema validation error' or 'duplicate key' messages, which often indicate an incomplete migration or misconfigured field mappings on the customer's side. 2. If duplicates are confirmed, run the standard data repair script to merge conflicting entries, but pause further imports until the root cause is resolved. 3. For configuration errors, guide the customer through the corrected mapping documentation to ensure source fields align with the current Mobile App provisioning schema. 4. If the issue stems from legacy data structures, a schema migration patch may be required to normalize the input before re-attempting the synchronization."
